; TitanProtocolEA.set
; Default input parameter template for mt5/TitanProtocolEA.mq5.
;
; This is a transport + execution bridge only -- it never generates,
; scores, or sizes trades. Replace ApiKey before attaching to any
; account; an empty key causes OnInit() to fail deliberately.
;
; ADR-034 Amendment 7: the EA's own compiled default for Transport is
; TRANSPORT_SOCKET (native MQL5 socket, bypasses WinINet/WebRequest()
; entirely) -- there is deliberately no Transport= line below, since
; this file's own personalization logic (install_mt5_files.py) cannot
; safely confirm MQL5's .set serialization format for a custom enum
; input without risking a silently-wrong value. Omitting it means MT5
; applies the compiled default (Socket) whenever this file is loaded.
; To roll back to HTTP, set Transport=Http explicitly in the EA's
; Inputs tab in MT5. SocketHost/SocketPort below are plain string/int
; inputs -- safe to personalize directly, and are filled in by
; install.py to match the live Bridge configuration's host/socket_port.

BackendUrl=http://127.0.0.1:8787
ApiKey=
HeartbeatIntervalSeconds=5
AllowedSymbolsCsv=
MagicNumber=20260710
MaxSlippagePoints=20
FailClosedTimeoutSeconds=30
EmergencyDisable=false
MaxRetries=3
RetryDelayMs=250
MaxRequoteRetries=2
RequoteRetryDelayMs=100
SocketHost=127.0.0.1
SocketPort=8788
SocketFailoverAfterAttempts=5
